---
const pressures = [
  {
    title: "How long will you keep betting nobody will bother to exploit your code?",
    description:
      "Attackers automate discovery too, and the odds get worse with every release. OpenTaint traces untrusted data to the operations it can damage, so the bet stops being a bet.",
    value: "Know what is reachable, not what is likely.",
  },
  {
    title: "Would you notice the agent slipping a vulnerability into code you never reviewed?",
    description:
      "The output can look finished and pass its tests while an untrusted value crosses helpers, fields, and libraries nobody read. OpenTaint reports the whole source-to-sink trace before that becomes invisible security debt.",
    value: "Generate fast. Verify before merge.",
  },
  {
    title: "Will your security agent review find tomorrow what it found today?",
    description:
      "An agent can find a pattern once, then miss it on the next nondeterministic review. OpenTaint records it as a versioned taint rule the engine applies on every scan.",
    value: "Turn every discovery into deterministic coverage.",
  },
  {
    title: "How much money will you waste on everything your security agent forgot it reviewed?",
    description:
      "Your last review already paid to learn the trust boundaries, the vulnerability patterns, and the opaque library behavior. Every scan that starts from zero buys all of it again.",
    value: "Spend tokens only when new context must be learned.",
  },
];
---

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="security-debt-heading">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <div>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-primary">Why now</p>
      <h2 id="security-debt-heading" class="section-heading mt-5">Application security is the new tech debt</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle max-w-[76ch]">
        AI makes code cheaper to produce and harder to fully review, so security work piles up in review queues and remediation backlogs. On the other side, autonomous agents now hunt for vulnerabilities at machine speed and at no meaningful cost: what used to take a skilled researcher a week takes a fleet of agents an afternoon, on every repository at once.
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* One text edge per question: the number sits in a gutter, the body runs
        in a single column, and only the conclusion breaks back out to the left. */}
    <ul class="mt-10 grid border-y border-border-strong md:grid-cols-2 lg:mt-14" aria-labelledby="security-debt-heading">
      {pressures.map((pressure, index) => (
        <li class:list={[
          "reveal grid grid-cols-[2.25rem_1fr] gap-y-3 py-7 md:py-9",
          index !== pressures.length - 1 && "border-b border-border",
          index === 2 && "md:border-b-0",
          index % 2 === 0 ? "md:pr-10" : "md:border-l md:border-border md:pl-10",
        ]}>
          <span class="pt-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[0.14em] text-primary">0{index + 1}</span>
          <h3 class="font-mono text-base font-semibold leading-7 text-foreground lg:text-[17px] lg:leading-[1.65]">{pressure.title}</h3>

          <p class="col-start-2 max-w-[54ch] font-mono text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">{pressure.description}</p>

          <p class="col-span-2 mt-2 self-end border-l-2 border-primary pl-3 font-mono text-xs font-semibold leading-5 text-foreground lg:text-sm lg:leading-6">{pressure.value}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
